{"_v":1,"id":"born-yesterday-1989","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Erik Haagensen","o":"Backstage","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.backstage.com/bso/reviews-ny-theatre-broadway/ny-review-born-yesterday-1005151992.story","q":"Definitely a play of its time, 'Born Yesterday' moves at a more leisurely pace than contemporary works and is unembarrassed by its idealized political message concerning a democracy's need for an informed citizenry. I hope that won't stop younger audiences from enjoying it. Me, I had a ball."}],"au":{"score":70,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":70,"c":8,"sr":3.5}}},"pd":"1989-01-18","ca":[{"n":"Edward Asner","r":"Harry Brock"},{"n":"Madeline Kahn","r":"Billie Dawn"},{"n":"Franklin Cover","r":"Ed Devery"},{"n":"Daniel Hugh Kelly","r":"Paul Verrall"},{"n":"Joel Bernstein","r":"Eddie Brock"},{"n":"Charlotte Booker","r":"A Manicurist"},{"n":"Peggy Cosgrave","r":"Mrs. Hedges"},{"n":"Heather Ehlers","r":"Helen"},{"n":"Paul Hebron","r":"Bellhop"},{"n":"Gregory Jbara","r":"A Bellhop"},{"n":"Ron Johnston","r":"The Assistant Manager"},{"n":"John Wylie","r":"Senator Norval Hedges"}]}